Decision 0003:
If the matching rules grow, move the filtering into a pure function in a new tutor_matching.py; update app.py to call it and adapt the subject-search test. This decision was made because find_tutors() in app.py handles the requests by Flasks, validates the subject, filters the sample tutor list,  and builds the JSON response in one function. One of the rejected lines is to do nothing because if we leave the file as is and we need to add more search filters later on it would be better to work on 1 file that handles it instead of working on a main file. The cost of doing this though would be to make another file that would be to only handle filtering and to make changes to the main file.
